    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "He had two wives. The name of one was Hannah, and the name of the other Peninnah. Peninnah had children, but Hannah had no children."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "but he gave a double portion to Hannah, for he loved Hannah, but the LORD had shut up her womb."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Elkanah her husband said to her, “Hannah, why do you weep? Why don’t you eat? Why is your heart grieved? Am I not better to you than ten sons?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Hannah rose up after they had finished eating and drinking in Shiloh. Now Eli the priest was sitting on his seat by the doorpost of the LORD’s temple."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Hannah spoke in her heart. Only her lips moved, but her voice was not heard. Therefore Eli thought she was drunk."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hannah answered, “No, my lord, I am a woman of a sorrowful spirit. I have not been drinking wine or strong drink, but I poured out my soul before the LORD."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "They rose up in the morning early and worshiped the LORD, then returned and came to their house to Ramah. Then Elkanah knew Hannah his wife; and the LORD remembered her."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the time had come, Hannah conceived, and bore a son; and she named him Samuel, saying, “Because I have asked him of the LORD.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 1:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Hannah didn’t go up, for she said to her husband, “Not until the child is weaned; then I will bring him, that he may appear before the LORD, and stay there forever.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 2:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hannah prayed, and said, “My heart exults in the LORD! My horn is exalted in the LORD. My mouth is enlarged over my enemies, because I rejoice in your salvation."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA 2:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD visited Hannah, and she conceived and bore three sons and two daughters. The child Samuel grew before the LORD."
      }
    ],
